45es|n|A pliant strip of wood or metal bent in a circular form, and united at the ends, for holding together the staves of casks, tubs, etc. ; A ring; a circular band; anything resembling a hoop, as the cylinder (cheese hoop) in which the curd is pressed in making cheese. ; A circle, or combination of circles, of thin whalebone, metal, or other elastic material, used for expanding the skirts of ladies' dresses; crinoline; -- used chiefly in the plural. ; A quart pot; -- so called because originally bound with hoops, like a barrel. Also, a portion of the contents measured by the distance between the hoops. ; An old measure of capacity, variously estimated at from one to four pecks. ; A shout; a whoop, as in whooping cough. ; The hoopoe. See Hoopoe.	a:47eq,177,97;45ee,149,2;45es,85,2;2rrc,79,1;1iv3,75,48;82g1,64,9;alsh,61,3;34jj,58,89;5q1g,57,8;a37k,55,13;9lm9,54,9;5txw,52,4;44ql,48,1;5lfu,46,5;abfv,45,10~47eq,177,97;34jj,58,89;1iv3,75,48;5yo3,3,29;4gr,34,19;a37k,55,13;wyo,24,11;abfv,45,10;5b7l,14,9;614m,1,9;82g1,64,9;9lm9,54,9;5q1g,57,8;53yv,15,7;4hyq,25,7	v:3c15,68,1;84wq,67,20;15fv,29,8~84wq,67,20;15fv,29,8;3c15,68,1	V:8qvc,104,4;4w3o,94,65;2qb4,88,1;94pg,65,2;8xn7,65,8;843b,62,13;8ljv,58,6;84wq,24,1;841v,22,2;u0q,18,4;68ew,8,5~4w3o,94,65;843b,62,13;8xn7,65,8;8ljv,58,6;68ew,8,5;8qvc,104,4;u0q,18,4;94pg,65,2;841v,22,2;2qb4,88,1;84wq,24,1	n:45ee,169,8;47eq,134,5;2udp,133,16;45es,124,30;ssg,118,63;2rrc,95,3;3c15,84,3;7ket,73,5;44ql,58,2;8mjr,55,3;8xn7,51,3;5r8m,51,11;2eu6,48,5;4n89,42,3;5txw,42,2~ssg,118,63;45es,124,30;2udp,133,16;9mne,11,14;akvv,40,12;5r8m,51,11;45ee,169,8;27n9,34,6;47eq,134,5;2eu6,48,5;7ket,73,5;76hf,41,3;2rrc,95,3;8xn7,51,3;34jj,9,3	N:8bmq,142,5;45es,124,30;8qvc,117,10;2qb4,104,3;94pg,98,20;9irf,89,9;4w3o,89,45;94pd,88,92;3ukz,84,5;24ys,73,8;ahcf,73,13;2j7h,70,7;945z,70,7;8445,63,9;464i,61,44~94pd,88,92;4w3o,89,45;464i,61,44;45es,124,30;94pg,98,20;8hz6,8,15;ahcf,73,13;7gis,17,13;5hu9,16,13;8qvc,117,10;9irf,89,9;8445,63,9;2kfq,37,8;24ys,73,8;1rui,53